//! The `border-top-width` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets the
//! width of the top border of an element.
//!
//! Initial: medium. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - medium: Same as `3px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-width
//! - thick: Same as `5px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-width
//! - thin: Same as `1px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-width
//!
//! Grammar: <line-width>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#propdef-border-top-width
